# Cloudflare Pages _redirects
# Rules apply in order — keep the referral retirement ABOVE the catch-alls.
#
# These rules DO fire despite _worker.js being present: the worker handles the
# routes it knows and calls env.ASSETS.fetch(request) for everything else, and
# _redirects is applied on that asset request. Verified 2026-08-20 — the worker
# carries no /refer or /dashboard route of its own.

# ─── Member account moved to the app (2026-08-20) ─────────────────────────
# The account layer moved to Platform A. /dashboard/ authenticates against
# Platform B and is NOT being repaired — it is the page being replaced.
#
# 85 links across 73 static pages still point at /dashboard: 63 building pages,
# the nav, /how-it-works/, /claim/, /petition.html, /welcome/, /buildings/,
# /intelligence/, /history/. This rule catches every one of them, which is why
# those hrefs are deliberately left alone rather than edited in 73 files.
#
# Unauthenticated arrivals land on the app's own sign-in. Do not add a
# /dashboard rule to _worker.js as well — two owners of one route is how a
# redirect loop starts.
/dashboard                 https://app.sanfranciscocondomarket.com/           301
/dashboard/                https://app.sanfranciscocondomarket.com/           301
/dashboard/*               https://app.sanfranciscocondomarket.com/           301

# ─── Account creation moved to the app (2026-08-20) ───────────────────────
# /save-10k/ called signInWithOtp against Platform B, which auto-creates the
# user. It was the ONLY member-facing account-creation surface left on B, and
# it took five real signups in the eight days after the merge cut — each one an
# account on the platform we are leaving, needing a manual migration and a
# forced password reset. This rule is what stops that.
#
# The confirm rule MUST stay above the splat: magic links already sitting in
# someone's inbox land on /save-10k/confirm/ and would otherwise be redirected
# mid-flow into a sign-in they cannot complete.
#
# The $10,000 pitch is not lost — the app's sign-in carries it. If the pitch
# page is wanted back as a page, the buildable version is to keep it and point
# its button at the app instead of calling B's auth.
/save-10k/confirm/*        /save-10k/confirm/index.html                       200
/save-10k                  https://app.sanfranciscocondomarket.com/signin     301
/save-10k/                 https://app.sanfranciscocondomarket.com/signin     301
/save-10k/*                https://app.sanfranciscocondomarket.com/signin     301

# ─── Referral programme retired (2026-07-28) ──────────────────────────────
# Condo Market cannot offer commission credit in exchange for referrals. The
# $10,000 is now a membership credit granted for creating an account.
#
# /refer/ is linked from the global nav and footer, from _worker.js (so it
# renders on every worker-rendered building page), and from historic emails.
# refer/index.html has been deleted, so these rules are what stop those 67
# inbound links 404ing. They must stay.
#
# These now chain: /refer/ -> /save-10k/ -> the app sign-in. Two hops is fine
# and keeps this block's documented behaviour intact; do not "optimise" it by
# repointing /refer/ at the app, or the retirement history stops being legible.
/refer                     /save-10k/         301
/refer/                    /save-10k/         301
/refer/*                   /save-10k/         301

# PM Partner Portal routing
/partner/                  /partner/index.html  200
/partner/*                 /partner/index.html  200

# Pretty-URL routing for building-scoped pages. The 200 status keeps the
# original URL in the address bar while serving the static HTML — pages
# themselves extract the slug from window.location.pathname.
/                          /buildings/        302

# HOA pitch deck — board-facing
/building/*/hoa-pitch/     /hoa-pitch.html    200
/building/*/hoa-pitch      /hoa-pitch.html    200

# Homeowner petition — owner-facing
/building/*/petition/      /petition.html     200
/building/*/petition       /petition.html     200

# Public partner portfolio pages — firm-facing
/partners/*/               /partners/index.html  200
/partners/*                /partners/index.html  200
